<description>
Flatten the interior object into a centered line and move the guide bars inward to bracket it.

Input structure:
- The dominant color is the background.
- One non-background guide color touches the boundary and forms exactly two full parallel bars plus a split perpendicular center bar.
- The other non-background color is a single 8-connected interior object whose area determines the flattened line length.

Rule:
- If the guide pair is vertical, make a vertical object-colored line centered between those bars; otherwise use the analogous horizontal line.
- The line length equals the number of interior object pixels and is centered on the split perpendicular guide bar.
- Rebuild the guide color as the perpendicular center bar plus two full bars immediately beside the flattened object line.

Key insight:
- The guide bars supply only the orientation and center; the interior object's pixel count supplies the length of the final one-cell-thick line.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "same-shape grid with a boundary-touching guide color forming two full parallel bars plus a split perpendicular center bar, and one 8-connected interior object color",
  "transform": "replace the scene with the guide color as the perpendicular center bar and two adjacent bars bracketing a one-cell object-colored line; orient the line parallel to the full guide-bar pair, center it on the perpendicular bar, and set its length to the interior object area"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: odd square NxN, N in 9-19
  colors: exactly 3 — background (7), guide (0), object (5) [observed: always these colors]
  guide_structure:
    parallel_pair: two full-spanning bars symmetric about grid center, even gap 4-8
    perpendicular_bar: spans entire axis EXCEPT between the parallel pair (split by object region)
    orientation: either vertical (full cols) or horizontal (full rows)
    all_centered: pair midpoint = perp bar position = grid center (N//2)
  object:
    color: does not touch grid boundary
    connectivity: single 8-connected component
    area: odd, range 5-13, must be <= N (fits as line along grid dimension)
    location: entirely between the parallel pair bars
    shape: arbitrary connected blob fitting within the gap interior
  output_structure:
    guide_rebuilt: perpendicular bar becomes full + parallel bars collapse to center-1 and center+1
    object_flattened: single-pixel-wide line of length=area, parallel to original pair, centered on perp bar
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick odd N (9-19), orientation (H or V), object area A (odd, 5 to N)
    2. Build output — center = N//2; place two full guide bars at center-1, center+1; place full perp bar at center; fill A pixels of object color centered on perp bar along center line
    3. Choose pair gap G (even, 4 to N-4, G >= ceil(sqrt(A))+2 to fit a blob); place parallel bars at center-G//2 and center+G//2
    4. Build input — keep the two parallel bars full, replace perp bar with split version (only outside parallel pair); generate a random 8-connected blob of area A fitting between the pair bars, then place it in the interior region
```
