<description>
Add a clipped direction-colored four-neighbor cross around each blue marker pixel.

Input structure
- The grid has a black background and one foreground color: blue marker pixels.
- Marker pixels are isolated enough that their four-neighbor stamps do not overlap or touch another marker.

Rule
- Keep every original blue marker pixel unchanged.
- For each marker, recolor its in-bounds background neighbor above to red, left to orange, right to pink, and below to teal.
- Clip the stamp at the grid boundary.

Key insight
- The marker position is an anchor; the added color is determined solely by compass direction from that anchor.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "isolated blue marker pixels on a black background",
  "transform": "preserve each marker; paint each in-bounds background neighbor by direction: above -> red, left -> orange, right -> pink, below -> teal"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 10x10 (fixed across all examples) [observed]
  background: BLACK
  markers:
    color: BLUE
    count: 5-7
    placement: anywhere on grid including edges/corners
    separation: no two crosses overlap; the 4-neighbor stamp of each marker
      (center + up/down/left/right) must be disjoint from every other stamp;
      equivalently manhattan_dist >= 3 for any pair, or chebyshev >= 2
      with additional manhattan check
    edge_markers: 2-4 markers may sit on grid boundary, clipping their cross
  transform:
    preserve: each BLUE marker pixel unchanged
    add_neighbors: |
      above -> RED(2), left -> ORANGE(7), right -> PINK(6), below -> TEAL(8)
      neighbors outside grid boundary are simply omitted (clipped)

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct placement (input-only; transform is trivial)
  steps:
    1. Create 10x10 BLACK grid
    2. Pick marker_count from 5-7
    3. Place markers one at a time at random positions; for each candidate,
       verify its full cross footprint (center + 4 neighbors clipped to bounds)
       does not overlap any already-placed cross footprint; reject and retry
       if overlap occurs
    4. Return the grid with only BLUE pixels at marker positions
  notes: >
    Rejection rate is low because 10x10 has 100 cells and each cross claims
    at most 5, so 7 crosses use at most 35 cells. Ensure at least one marker
    sits on an edge/corner for variety (soft goal).
```
</generation_spec>
