<description>
Draw the selected diagonal marker segment, then let any blockers on it emit perpendicular diagonals.

Input structure
A mostly background grid with sparse foreground marker pixels. Among same-color
marker pairs, exactly one diagonal pair is the primary segment: it is the pair
whose segment contains the most differently colored foreground markers.

Rule
Paint the primary diagonal segment in its endpoint color, preserving any
differently colored markers already on that segment. Each preserved marker on
the segment paints the full perpendicular diagonal across the grid in its own
color. Other foreground markers stay unchanged.

Key insight
The differently colored markers on the primary diagonal are blockers for the
primary line and also control pixels for perpendicular line emission.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "same-color diagonal marker pair s and other-color marker/control pixels on s.segment",
  "path": "connect s by its 45-degree diagonal segment; each control pixel on that segment casts the perpendicular 45-degree diagonal to both grid edges",
  "trajectory": "paint s.color along the segment and each control pixel's color along its full perpendicular diagonal",
  "transform": "preserve control pixels on the primary segment and keep all off-path foreground markers unchanged",
  "multi_step": "select the unique same-color diagonal pair whose segment contains the most other-color markers, paint that segment, then emit perpendicular diagonals from the preserved markers"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 8-19 rows x 9-16 cols, uniform background (any non-fg color)
  colors: exactly 2 foreground colors -- line_col (always 1 [observed]) and blocker_col (always 6 [observed])
  segment:
    two endpoint pixels of line_col on a strict 45-degree diagonal (|dr|==|dc|, dr!=0)
    segment length (inclusive): 6-10 cells
    endpoints not on grid edges; at least 1 cell margin from each border
  blockers:
    0-2 pixels of blocker_col placed on interior cells of the segment (not at endpoints)
    the segment must be the unique diagonal pair across ALL fg pixels with the most blockers
  distractors:
    0-5 additional fg pixels (either color) scattered on background
    not on the primary segment, not on any perpendicular diagonal emitted by blockers
    must not form any same-color diagonal pair whose segment contains >= primary's blocker count
  output:
    paint line_col along the entire primary segment (preserving blocker pixels)
    each blocker emits a full perpendicular 45-degree diagonal across the grid in blocker_col
    all distractors remain unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims (H 8-19, W 9-16), bg color, line_col, blocker_col (all distinct).
    2. Choose a 45-degree diagonal direction from {(1,1),(1,-1)}.
    3. Pick segment length L (6-10). Place two endpoint pixels of line_col such that
       the segment fits with >=1 cell margin from all edges.
    4. Place 0-2 blocker_col pixels on interior segment cells.
    5. Compute perpendicular diagonals from each blocker; verify they only cross bg cells.
    6. Build the output: fill segment with line_col, fill perp diags with blocker_col.
    7. Derive input from output: erase the segment (restore bg) except at the two
       endpoints and blocker positions. Erase perpendicular diagonal pixels (restore bg)
       except at blocker positions.
    8. Optionally place 0-5 distractor pixels on cells that are bg in both input and output,
       not on the segment line or any perp diagonal. Verify no same-color diagonal pair
       among all fg pixels matches or exceeds primary blocker count.
```
</generation_spec>
</reference_puzzle>

