<description>
Slide each foreground object horizontally to the edge indicated by whether its shape has an open notch.

Input structure:
- Yellow is the background and there is one blue foreground color.
- The foreground is split into separated 4-connected objects.
- Each object keeps its row span and shape in the output.

Rule:
- If an object's bbox border contains a background gap flanked by object pixels along that same border, slide it to the right edge and recolor it green.
- Otherwise slide the object to the left edge and recolor it red.
- Start from a blank background canvas; no moved objects overlap.

Key insight:
- The target side is encoded by the object's shape, not by its original position: open notches go right, while closed or solid shapes go left.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "4-connected blue foreground objects",
  "path": "horizontal slide in the same rows to the selected grid edge",
  "dst": "left edge for closed or solid objects; right edge for objects with a flanked open notch on the bbox border",
  "trajectory": "translate the whole object without changing its shape",
  "transform": "recolor left-moving objects red and right-moving objects green"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 22 rows (constant) x 19-26 cols
  background: yellow (4)
  foreground_color: blue (1) — single color for all objects in input
  objects:
    count: 3-5 total; always exactly 2 with open notch + 1-3 without [observed]
    shape: 4-connected blobs; bbox 2-6 rows x 2-9 cols; fill ratio 64-100%
    notch_definition: |
      bbox border has a bg gap flanked by filled cells on same border edge
      (top/bottom row or left/right column of the bounding box)
      No-notch shapes may still have interior holes or corner gaps, but no flanked border gap
    row_spans: all objects have mutually non-overlapping row spans; gap >= 1 row between consecutive objects
    input_placement: objects placed in interior columns (not touching left/right edge) [observed]
  transformation:
    notch_objects: slide right to right grid edge, recolor green (3)
    no_notch_objects: slide left to left grid edge, recolor red (2)
    row_span preserved; shape preserved; output starts from blank bg canvas
    no overlap after sliding (guaranteed by non-overlapping row spans)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid width W in 19-26; height is always 22
    2. Pick N=3-5 objects; assign exactly 2 as notch (right/green), rest as no-notch (left/red)
    3. For each object, design its mask within a bbox of 2-6 rows x 2-9 cols (w < W/2):
       - notch objects: ensure at least one bg gap flanked by filled cells on a bbox border edge
       - no-notch objects: ensure NO flanked border gap (solid, frame with only interior/corner holes)
       - object must be a single 4-connected component; fill >= 60%
    4. Assign non-overlapping row spans to all objects with >= 1 row gap; must fit in 22 rows
    5. Place each object at its output edge position (left col=0 or right col=W-w) — this is the output
    6. To create input: move each object to a random interior column position (away from both edges),
       recolor all from red/green back to blue (1), paint onto a blank yellow grid
